{
  "scenarioId": "s01-greetings",
  "title": "Greetings and small talk",
  "subtitle": "Meeting people and getting by in everyday conversation",
  "registerPolicy": "Two spoken registers only: casual (nee, un-, -a/-iya endings) and respectful (neenga, unga-, -eenga/-unga endings). Written or formal-literary forms (neengal, -irgal, medhuvaaga) are out of scope. 'neutral' = the sentence has no you-form, so no register choice is needed. Casual items may end in da (male friend) or di (female friend); `addressee` records which.",
  "romanisationNote": "PROVISIONAL informal Latin spelling as used in Tamil WhatsApp chats; final scheme open (OPEN_ITEMS, Task 0.3). Variants are listed in acceptedAnswers.",
